# The car's two screens: which monitor shows what. docs/car-screens.md.
# Read by tools/car_screen.sh, which aav-hud.service and aav-map.service run at login.
# Installed to ~/.config/aav/screens.env by tools/car_screens_install.sh: edit it there,
# then: systemctl --user restart aav-hud aav-map
#
# One KEY=value a line, nothing else: no spaces around =, no $VARIABLES, no ~.
#
# The monitors: the name exactly as this prints it (on X11, the same names as
# `xrandr --listmonitors`: HDMI-1, HDMI-2, DSI-1...), or the number it shows (0 = the first):
#   ~/aav-jazzy/aav.sh tools/car_screen.sh --list
# Empty: that screen doesn't start, and its journal says why.
AAV_HUD_MONITOR=
AAV_MAP_MONITOR=
# Our ROS network: the car's stack is on 42 (aav.sh). A Mac watching sets the same.
AAV_ROS_DOMAIN_ID=42
# The map window's offline files (the car kit copies them; else pixi run get street-map
# and pixi run get places). Empty: config/map.yaml's, maps/... in the code's folder.
AAV_STREET_MAP=@PREFIX@/aav/maps/streets/ottawa.pmtiles
AAV_PLACES=@PREFIX@/aav/maps/places/ottawa.db
